	(text "Click a box on the left to open its page. \"Contents\" and the page numbers at the bottom right of\nevery page lead back here and to each page.\n\nCyan lines are connections: wires and pin ends, all one width. A dot joins lines; a cross on a pin\nend means the pin is not connected. Pins connect by net labels (the boxed names): pins whose labels\ncarry the same name are on one net, on any page. [3/C4] after a label: page 3 carries that net too,\nits label in zone C4 (column 4, row C of the border). Click it to land on that label. No [page/zone]:\nthe net is on this page only. Click a part's reference to find its row in the parts list; the row's\npage/zone leads back. A part crossed out in red is not fitted (DNP). White: parts and their\nreferences. Grey: values, pin names, pin numbers. A dashed frame is a block of the circuit, titled\nat its top left. An amber K3 marks a Kleidos addition or correction: it leads to its row below."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 215.9 45.085 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.75 1.75)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "29a6f9e1-5ccd-50da-b8f4-2be8cfd2db88")
	)
	(text "Notes"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 215.9 84.16 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
